# icu -- ICU4C, the Unicode and internationalisation library SpiderMonkey is
# built against.
#
# Packaged because of --with-system-icu, and that flag is not a preference.
# SpiderMonkey vendors its own copy of ICU, and a vendored ICU inside
# libmozjs-140.so would put a SECOND full Unicode implementation into every
# GNOME Shell process -- one exporting the same symbol names as the system one
# that gtk4, harfbuzz and pango reach through their own chain. BLFS says of the
# --with-system-* switches only that they "are required for stability"; the
# concrete version of that is two ICUs in one address space, where the loader
# resolves each symbol to whichever library it reaches first.
#
# js/moz.configure asks for `icu-uc icu-i18n >= 76.1` (line 1196, guarded by
# --with-system-icu). 77.1 is BLFS 12.4's pin and satisfies it.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/unicode-org/icu/releases/download/release-77-1/icu4c-77_1-src.tgz
SRC_SHA256=588e431f77327c39031ffbb8843c0e3bc122c211374485fa87dc5f3faff24061
SRC_DIR=icu

# The tarball unpacks to a bare `icu/`, not to `icu-77.1/`, and the configure
# script is one level further down in `icu/source/`. Both facts are why this
# recipe carries its own build and install stages: the generic ones look for
# $SRC_PATH/configure and would find a directory.
#
# SRC_DIR is therefore `icu` and the version appears nowhere in it -- see the
# note in check-recipes.sh's version_forms about the `77_1` spelling, which this
# package is the reason for.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-samples --disable-tests"
